https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YDhLh4yok90  (Capo 1) (MC0)

TIP:  There’s also a version in C in case you don’t like the (Bm).

TIP:  For the opening play a regular (D) and extend your pinky over to the 1st string of the 5th fret to cover note <a>.  Strum aiming for the open 4th string <d> and then strum down to snap the 1st string.  Repeat.  Or ignore it and just play (D).

TIP:  If transposing, play the transposed (DaddA) root chord and add the 5th note if needed.
     

